{
  "$comment": "One table, two implementations of what a collection hides of an entry (domain-model.md §2, 'Narrowing hides, it never deletes'). The Go domain (core/domain/model/work/StructureEntries.go) decides it for every read and refuses the writes it names; the web app (apps/webapp/src/lib/data/replica.ts) derives the same mark for what it answers from the replica. `bound` is what GET /meta/capabilities answers as item_types; `structure` is a container's structure in force, as `structure.settings` carries its levels and fields; `ancestors` are the types above the entry, nearest first; `hidden` is WorkItem.hidden. `below` holds a tree of entries (`parent` null for a task, `trashed` for one in the trash) under several structures; its `below` is WorkItem.hidden.below of each entry, an entry not named counting none.",
